      "takeaway_fil": "Ang plano ay may taong kikilos at paraan upang malaman kung bumaba ang hadlang.",
      "takeaway_en": "A plan names who acts and how to tell whether the barrier decreased.",
      "check": {
        "prompt_fil": "Nagawa ang meeting ngunit hindi dumami ang nakarating. Ano ang tamang review?",
        "prompt_en": "The meeting happened but attendance did not improve. What review is useful?",
        "options": [
          {
            "fil": "Ituring na tagumpay dahil natapos ang meeting.",
            "en": "Declare success because the meeting finished."
          },
          {
            "fil": "Ulitin ang parehong plano nang walang bagong tanong.",
            "en": "Repeat the same plan without new questions."
          },
          {
            "fil": "Balikan ang hadlang at ihambing ang invitations at attendance bago magbago.",
            "en": "Recheck barriers and compare invitations with attendance before revising."
          }
        ],
        "correct_option_index": 2,
        "feedback_fil": "Una: ang natapos na meeting ay gawain, hindi patunay ng pagtaas ng attendance o pagkawala ng hadlang. Ikalawa: ang pag-uulit nang walang bagong tanong ay maaaring ulitin ang maling palagay; kailangan ang bagong ebidensya. Ikatlo: tama—balikan ang hadlang at ihambing ang invitations at attendance. Bago: 1 sa 3; pagkatapos: 1 sa 3. Dalawa pa rin ang hindi nakapunta. Rebisadong plano ni Carole: sanhi—kumpirmadong trabaho at pag-aalaga, ngunit hindi pa alam ang dahilan ng bawat hindi pagdalo; mungkahi—muling konsultasyon bago magtalakay ng maliit na trial; owner—Carole sa konsultasyon at health team sa desisyon sa schedule; resources—papel at oras, staff time na hinihintay; deadline—pagtalakay sa Biyernes; sukatan—attendance sa inimbitahan at dahilan ng hindi pagdalo; review—Lunes pagkatapos ng napagkasunduang trial. Trial date at ambag ay hinihintay pa sa katuwang. Walang pangako ng pondo o pagkalutas ng buong problema.",
        "feedback_en": "First: a completed meeting is an activity, not proof of increased attendance or removal of a barrier. Second: repeating without new questions may repeat a mistaken assumption; new evidence is needed. Third: correct—recheck barriers and compare invitations with attendance. Before: 1 of 3; after: 1 of 3. Two still missed visits. Carole’s revised plan: cause—confirmed work and childcare barriers, but each reason for nonattendance remains unknown; proposal—consult again before discussing a small trial; owner—Carole for consultation and the health team for schedule decisions; resources—paper and time, with staff time pending; deadline—Friday discussion; measure—attendance among those invited and reasons for missing visits; review—Monday after an agreed trial. Trial date and contributions still await partner agreement. No funding or resolution of the whole problem is promised."
      }
    }
